<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33407" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pāla</span></b> , ae, f.
		contr. from pagela, from pago, pango: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pala a pangendo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 134</span></i>
			 Müll., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a spade.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palas vendundas sibi ait ... ut hortum fodiat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 5, 2, 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sarcula VIII., palas IV.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 10, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palae innixus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 3,
					26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juncosus ager verti pala debet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 6, 8, § 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palis laxatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					17, 17, 27, § 123</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 10, 45</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A peel</i> for putting bread into the oven,
					<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A winnowing-shovel</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Tert. Praescr. 3</span></i>; so
					<i><span class="en">Juvenc. 1,
			371</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>The bezel</i> of a ring = funda: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palam anuli ad palmam convertere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 3, 9, 38</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<i>The shoulder-blade</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Acut. 2, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Tard. 3, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<i>An Indian tree</i>, <i>the
				plantain-tree</i>: Musa Paradisiaca, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 12, 6,
				12, § 24</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
